# Day 05 — Linux Services & systemd

## 📌 Topics Covered

Today I learned how Linux services are managed using systemd and practiced service troubleshooting.

### 1. Linux Services

A service is a background component that provides a specific function, such as:

* SSH
* Nginx
* Apache
* MySQL
* Docker
* Cron

### 2. systemd

Learned that systemd is a system and service manager used by many modern Linux distributions.

Checked:

```bash
ps -p 1 -f
systemctl --version
```

### 3. systemctl

Practiced:

```bash
systemctl status SERVICE
systemctl start SERVICE
systemctl stop SERVICE
systemctl restart SERVICE
systemctl reload SERVICE
```

### 4. Enable and Disable Services

Learned the difference between starting a service immediately and configuring it to start automatically.

```bash
systemctl enable SERVICE
systemctl disable SERVICE
systemctl enable --now SERVICE
```

Also learned about:

```bash
systemctl mask SERVICE
systemctl unmask SERVICE
```

### 5. Service Monitoring

Practiced:

```bash
systemctl is-active SERVICE
systemctl is-enabled SERVICE
systemctl --failed
systemctl list-units --type=service
systemctl list-unit-files --type=service
```

### 6. Nginx Hands-on

Installed and managed Nginx as a practical example.

Practiced:

```bash
sudo systemctl start nginx
sudo systemctl status nginx
sudo systemctl restart nginx
sudo systemctl reload nginx
sudo systemctl enable nginx
```

Verified the web server:

```bash
curl -I http://localhost
```

### 7. Service Logs with journalctl

Practiced:

```bash
sudo journalctl -u nginx
sudo journalctl -u nginx -n 50
sudo journalctl -u nginx -f
sudo journalctl -u nginx -b
```

Learned how `journalctl` can be used to investigate service failures and runtime events.

### 8. Nginx Configuration Validation

Before reloading/restarting after configuration changes:

```bash
sudo nginx -t
```

This validates the Nginx configuration syntax.

### 9. Port and Service Troubleshooting

Checked listening ports:

```bash
sudo ss -lntp
```

Specifically checked HTTP port 80:

```bash
sudo ss -lntp | grep ':80'
```

### 10. systemd Unit Files

Inspected service definitions:

```bash
systemctl cat nginx
```

Learned about common systemd unit locations:

```text
/etc/systemd/system/
/usr/lib/systemd/system/
/lib/systemd/system/
```

### 11. Service Troubleshooting Flow

When a service is unavailable:

```text
Service unavailable
        ↓
systemctl status
        ↓
journalctl
        ↓
Validate configuration
        ↓
Check ports/dependencies
        ↓
Fix root cause
        ↓
Reload/restart
        ↓
Verify
```

### 🎯 Key Commands

```bash
systemctl status SERVICE
systemctl start SERVICE
systemctl stop SERVICE
systemctl restart SERVICE
systemctl reload SERVICE

systemctl enable SERVICE
